{% comment %}
  What "Ka" means - the brand's thesis, from Santosh's brand overview doc.

  This exists because the site already carries the idea everywhere and never
  explains it: the rail of letterforms running down the side of every page, and
  the ring of symbols around the cup in the logo, are the same thing - the
  letter "ka" written in thirteen Indian scripts. Without a word of explanation
  a visitor reads them as decoration. With it, they're the reason the company
  has this name.

  The glyphs are the same thirteen the rail uses, rendered from
  snippets/ka-rail-icon.liquid so there is one source of truth: change a
  letterform there and it changes in both places.

  On scale: each glyph carries an inline width/height that sizes it to a shared
  566px^2 area rather than a shared box, because fitting a wide glyph and a tall
  one into the same square shrinks them by very different amounts and Santosh
  flagged that some scripts were reading smaller than others. Scaling every
  glyph by one factor keeps that balance exactly, so this uses `zoom` - which,
  unlike `transform: scale()`, actually takes part in layout, so the grid still
  flows. The @supports fallback is for browsers without it: the glyphs stay
  small but readable rather than vanishing.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  The letterform backdrop rides on the theme's own section-background element,
  which is already exactly viewport-wide and absolutely positioned, so the
  artwork gets its full bleed for free.

  It ships as an alpha mask rather than a picture - see
  scripts/build-ka-pattern.py - so the glyphs take whatever colour is set
  under them rather than one baked into a PNG. One file serves a blush field
  on white here and a cream one on a dark band, with no second asset.

  The colour is its own setting rather than the scheme's foreground: a
  backdrop is a flat colour of its own, and reaching it by fading the text
  colour down gives a grey of that hue, never the blush this wants.

  The URL has to be handed to the CSS from here: the stylesheet block below
  is static and never sees Liquid, so asset_url can't be written inside it.

  Do not write that block's opening tag in a comment, here or anywhere else
  in a section. Shopify pulls the CSS out by scanning the raw file for the
  tag, and a comment is still raw text to that scan - so the first one it
  finds wins and everything after it, markup and script included, is
  compiled into styles.css as if it were CSS. The browser then throws the
  whole run away and the section renders unstyled, while the file looks
  perfectly correct.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="section-background color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} why-ka__bg{% if section.settings.show_pattern %} why-ka__bg--pattern{% endif %}"
  {%- if section.settings.show_pattern %}
    style="--ka-pattern: url('{{ 'ka-pattern.png' | asset_url }}'); --ka-pattern-opacity: {{ section.settings.pattern_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};{% if section.settings.pattern_color != blank %} --ka-pattern-ink: {{ section.settings.pattern_color }};{% endif %}"
  {%- endif %}
></div>
<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} why-ka spacing-style"
  style="{%- render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
>
  <div class="why-ka__inner">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="why-ka__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <div class="why-ka__body rte">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The glyph grid sits outside __inner so it can use the section's full width.
    Inside the text column it left a void to the right of every paragraph.

    Behind a setting because the homepage currently runs without it - Santosh
    is working on something to put in its place - while Our Story still shows
    the full specimen sheet. The caption is inside the same condition: on its
    own it describes letters that aren't there.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_glyphs -%}
    <div class="why-ka__glyphs" role="img" aria-label="{{ section.settings.glyph_alt | escape }}">
      {%- for i in (0..12) -%}
        <span class="why-ka__glyph">{%- render 'ka-rail-icon', index: i -%}</span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.caption != blank -%}
      <p class="why-ka__caption">{{ section.settings.caption }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The atlas: the twelve languages on the left, and on the right the one you
    picked, written large in its own script, over the states where it is the
    language people actually speak.

    The table below is reference data, not copy, which is why it is here rather
    than in the schema. Each row is: the glyph's index in
    snippets/ka-rail-icon.liquid (labelled there), the regions to light in
    assets/south-asia-map.svg, and what to say about the places the map cannot
    show.

    That last column is the whole reason this is honest. The map has Indian
    states as separate shapes and everything beyond India as a single outline,
    so there is no way to fill Pakistan for Urdu or Bangladesh for Bengali -
    and filling a whole country for a language would be a claim none of these
    deserve anyway. Those are said in words instead, under the map, and no
    national border is drawn anywhere on it.

    The map predates Telangana, so Andhra Pradesh is undivided here. For Telugu
    that is right either way; for Urdu it is why Andhra Pradesh is in its list.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign atlas = 'Hindi|3|uttar_pradesh,madhya_pradesh,bihar,rajasthan,haryana,jharkhand,chhattisgarh,uttaranchal,himachal_pradesh,delhi_ncr|Nepali, its close cousin, is the national language of Nepal.
Tamil|8|tamil_nadu,pudducherry_pondicherry,karikal_pondicherry|Also official in Sri Lanka and Singapore.
Telugu|2|andhra_pradesh,yanam_pondicherry|
Kannada|9|karnataka|
Malayalam|5|kerala,mahe_pondicherry|
Bengali-Assamese|0|west_bengal,assam,tripura|Bengali is the national language of Bangladesh.
Gujarati|4|gujarat,dadra_and_nagar_haveli,diu|
Odia|6|orissa|
Punjabi|7|punjab,chandigarh,haryana|Punjabi is spoken across the border in Pakistan too, written in a different script.
Urdu|10|jammu_and_kashmir,uttar_pradesh,bihar,delhi_ncr,andhra_pradesh|The national language of Pakistan.
Meitei|11|manipur|
Santali|12|jharkhand,orissa,west_bengal,assam,bihar|' | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}

  <div class="why-ka__atlas" id="why-ka-atlas-{{ section.id }}" data-map="{{ 'south-asia-map.svg' | asset_url }}">
    <ul class="why-ka__languages" role="tablist" aria-label="Languages">
      {%- for row in atlas -%}
        {%- assign cell = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
        {%- if cell[0] != blank -%}
          <li>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="why-ka__language{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}"
              role="tab"
              aria-selected="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
              data-lang="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
              data-regions="{{ cell[2] | strip }}"
              data-where="{{ cell[3] | strip | escape }}"
            >
              {{- cell[0] | strip -}}
            </button>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    <div class="why-ka__plate">
      <div class="why-ka__letters">
        {%- for row in atlas -%}
          {%- assign cell = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
          {%- if cell[0] != blank -%}
            <span
              class="why-ka__letter{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}"
              data-letter="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              {%- render 'ka-rail-icon', index: cell[1] -%}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      <div class="why-ka__map" data-map-slot></div>
    </div>

    <p class="why-ka__where" data-where-out aria-live="polite">
      {%- assign first = atlas[0] | strip | split: '|' -%}
      {{- first[3] | strip -}}
    </p>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.closing != blank -%}
    <p class="why-ka__closing">{{ section.settings.closing }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<script>
  (() => {
    const root = document.getElementById('why-ka-atlas-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root || root.dataset.ready) return;
    root.dataset.ready = 'true';

    const buttons = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('[data-lang]'));
    const letters = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('[data-letter]'));
    const slot = root.querySelector('[data-map-slot]');
    const where = root.querySelector('[data-where-out]');
    if (!buttons.length || !slot) return;

    /*
      The map is fetched rather than inlined into the page.

      It is 60KB of path data for one section most visitors will scroll past,
      so it waits until the section is near the viewport and then arrives once
      and stays cached. asset_url is same-origin, so there is no CORS in it.

      Inlined rather than used as <img> because the whole point is to fill
      individual states, and CSS cannot reach inside an <img>.
    */
    let loaded = false;
    const load = async () => {
      if (loaded) return;
      loaded = true;
      try {
        const res = await fetch(root.dataset.map);
        if (!res.ok) return;
        slot.innerHTML = await res.text();
        const svg = slot.querySelector('svg');
        if (svg) svg.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
        paint(buttons.find((b) => b.classList.contains('is-on')) || buttons[0]);
      } catch {
        /* the letters and the list still work; the map is the enhancement */
      }
    };

    const paint = (button) => {
      if (!button) return;
      slot.querySelectorAll('.is-lit').forEach((el) => el.classList.remove('is-lit'));
      (button.dataset.regions || '')
        .split(',')
        .map((r) => r.trim())
        .filter(Boolean)
        .forEach((r) => {
          const el = slot.querySelector('#kcc-map-' + r);
          if (el) el.classList.add('is-lit');
        });
    };

    const show = (button) => {
      buttons.forEach((b) => {
        const on = b === button;
        b.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
        b.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
      const i = button.dataset.lang;
      letters.forEach((l) => l.classList.toggle('is-on', l.dataset.letter === i));
      if (where) where.textContent = button.dataset.where || '';
      paint(button);
    };

    buttons.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => show(b)));

    /*
      Left and right walk the list the way a tablist is expected to, so the
      twelve are not twelve separate tab stops between the copy and the rest
      of the page.
    */
    root.querySelector('[role="tablist"]').addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      const step = e.key === 'ArrowRight' ? 1 : e.key === 'ArrowLeft' ? -1 : 0;
      if (!step) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      const at = buttons.indexOf(document.activeElement);
      const next = buttons[(at + step + buttons.length) % buttons.length];
      next.focus();
      show(next);
    });

    if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
      const io = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => entries.forEach((en) => { if (en.isIntersecting) { io.disconnect(); load(); } }),
        { rootMargin: '400px 0px' }
      );
      io.observe(root);
    } else {
      load();
    }
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  .why-ka__bg {
    position: relative;
  }

  /* A wave divider is its own section, and the part of it below the curve is
     flat background - so a field that starts at this section's own top edge
     leaves a bare strip between the trough of the wave and the first glyph,
     which reads as a gap rather than as a margin. The field rises by the
     wave's height and is covered by its solid fill, so it starts at the curve
     itself. The rise is the wave's own svg height; see snippets/wave-divider. */
  #MainContent > div.shopify-section:has(.wave-divider) + div.shopify-section .why-ka__bg--pattern {
    --ka-pattern-rise: 72px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    #MainContent > div.shopify-section:has(.wave-divider) + div.shopify-section .why-ka__bg--pattern {
      --ka-pattern-rise: 124px;
    }
  }

  /* The mask is what makes this a texture rather than a picture: the PNG
     carries only an alpha channel, and the colour under it is the scheme's
     own foreground, so the glyphs come out cream on the dark band and brown
     on a light one without a second file.

     `cover` rather than a tile. The artwork is one composition, not a
     repeating unit - its edges cut through letterforms, so repeating it would
     draw a seam straight down the section. One copy, cropped. */
  .why-ka__bg--pattern::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    top: calc(-1 * var(--ka-pattern-rise, 0px));
    background-color: var(--ka-pattern-ink, var(--color-foreground, currentColor));
    -webkit-mask-image: var(--ka-pattern);
    mask-image: var(--ka-pattern);
    -webkit-mask-size: cover;
    mask-size: cover;
    -webkit-mask-position: center;
    mask-position: center;
    -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    opacity: var(--ka-pattern-opacity, 0.12);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Sized to the prose itself, so the text column has no orphan space beside
     it. The glyph grid is a sibling and uses the section's full width. */
  .why-ka__inner {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .why-ka__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: var(--kcc-h2);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .why-ka__body p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: var(--kcc-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .why-ka__body p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  /* The thirteen letterforms, as a specimen sheet. Centred because the point
     is the set, not any one of them. */
  .why-ka__glyphs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    margin-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-primary, currentColor);
  }

  .why-ka__glyph {
    display: inline-flex;
    /* Preserves the per-glyph equal-area sizing set in ka-rail-icon.liquid;
       see the comment at the top of this file. */
    zoom: 3.4;
  }

  @supports not (zoom: 2) {
    .why-ka__glyph svg {
      height: 4.25rem;
      width: auto;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .why-ka__glyph {
      zoom: 2.4;
    }

    @supports not (zoom: 2) {
      .why-ka__glyph svg {
        height: 3rem;
      }
    }
  }

  .why-ka__caption {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--kcc-small);
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .why-ka__closing {
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: var(--kcc-h3);
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) auto 0;
    max-width: 30rem;
  }
  /* ---- The atlas ------------------------------------------------------- */

  .why-ka__atlas {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    margin-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .why-ka__atlas {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.38fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    }
  }

  .why-ka__languages {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .why-ka__languages {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.1rem;
    }
  }

  /* Set in the heading face, because this list is the specimen as much as the
     letter beside it is: twelve names, one per script. */
  .why-ka__language {
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.65rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 2.2vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
    opacity: 0.45;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: start;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .why-ka__language {
      padding-inline: 0;
    }
  }

  .why-ka__language:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .why-ka__language.is-on {
    opacity: 1;
    color: var(--kcc-ingredient-selected, #2e6417);
  }

  .why-ka__language:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* The letter and the map share a cell, the letter behind the map at a size
     that makes it the ground rather than an ornament on it. */
  /* The letter and the map share one square cell: the drawing of the letter
     is the ground the map is printed on, which is the whole idea - the shape
     and the place are the same fact told twice. Capped, because at full column
     width the map swamps the list beside it. */
  .why-ka__plate {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-areas: 'plate';
    align-items: center;
    justify-items: center;
    inline-size: 100%;
    max-inline-size: 32rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .why-ka__letters,
  .why-ka__map {
    grid-area: plate;
    inline-size: 100%;
  }

  .why-ka__letters {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /* The box has to be given a size, not left to its content: the glyph below
     is sized as a percentage of it, and a percentage of an auto height
     resolves to auto - which is why the letter was not there at all. */
  .why-ka__letter {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    color: var(--kcc-ingredient-selected, #2e6417);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.22s ease;
  }

  .why-ka__letter.is-on {
    opacity: 0.3;
  }

  .why-ka__letter svg {
    inline-size: auto;
    block-size: 78%;
    max-inline-size: 86%;
  }

  .why-ka__map svg {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Every region outlined, none filled, until one is. A hairline that does not
     thicken as the map scales, so the whole subcontinent keeps one pen. */
  .why-ka__map .kcc-map__region {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1;
    vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
    opacity: 0.3;
    transition: fill 0.25s ease, opacity 0.25s ease;
  }

  .why-ka__map .kcc-map__region.is-lit {
    fill: currentColor;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .why-ka__letter,
    .why-ka__map .kcc-map__region {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  .why-ka__where {
    margin: 0.75rem auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    min-block-size: 2.8em;
    max-inline-size: 26rem;
    font-size: var(--kcc-small);
    line-height: 1.5;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Why Ka",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Every Indian language begins with the same letter" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_glyphs", "label": "Show the letterform specimen sheet", "info": "The thirteen scripts and their caption, under the text.", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "glyph_alt", "label": "Glyph grid description", "default": "The letter ka, written in thirteen Indian scripts" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption under the letters" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "closing", "label": "Closing line" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_pattern",
      "label": "Letterform backdrop",
      "info": "The field of ka glyphs behind the section, painted in the scheme's own text colour.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "pattern_color",
      "label": "Backdrop colour",
      "info": "The colour the letterforms are drawn in. Left empty, they take the scheme's text colour.",
      "default": "#f7ebe7"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "pattern_opacity",
      "label": "Backdrop strength",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-2" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "Width",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page-width", "label": "Page" },
        { "value": "full-width", "label": "Full" }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 80 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 160, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 80 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Why Ka" }]
}
{% endschema %}



